  <prompt>
    Root-cause and fix the mount-state reset on the transient/upload path so "Restore from Source" restores content instead of
    blanking the page and asking for re-upload. This is the same lifecycle as the FR-07(c) mount-identity vector (task 011).
  </prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in the Compose transient/upload mount state machine. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>
    "Restore from Source" restores the document content without blanking the page or requiring re-upload.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      spec.md FR-09 (R6 D4). Not root-caused in R6. Same mount-state reset lifecycle as FR-07 vector b/c (task 011 output informs this).
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeWorkspace.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">ComposeWorkspace.types.ts mountTransient@559 / mountDraftHtml@613 (speDriveItemId/mount-state reset) — the lifecycle to root-cause</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">Task 011 mount-identity fixes (reuse findings on which mount doors reset state)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="011" status="pending">Mount-identity root-cause — 011 maps the transient mount doors that reset state; reuse that analysis.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Root-cause the mount-state reset on the transient/upload path (the FR-07 vector-b/c lifecycle); the fix MUST restore content without re-upload. Reuse task-011's mount-door analysis; MUST NOT add a parallel restore path (root §11).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">MUST NOT delete docxBridge.ts. MUST NOT regress the transient/draft mount behaviors fixed in 010/011.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>compose mount lifecycle, restore from source</topic>
