  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare rigor FULL, effort xhigh; load spec FR-09 + task-011 mount-door analysis.</step>
    <step order="1">Reproduce the blank-on-restore; trace the transient/upload mount-state reset (mountTransient@559 / mountDraftHtml@613).</step>
    <step order="2">Root-cause the reset and fix so Restore from Source restores content without re-upload.</step>
    <step order="3">Add unit tests: Restore from Source restores content; no re-upload prompt; no blank.</step>
    <step order="4">Run jest + ui-tests; verify green + no regression to 010/011 behaviors.</step>
    <step order="5">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set 071 status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="6">Document the root cause in projects/spaarkeai-compose-r7/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the root cause turns out to require a server round-trip to restore source content (not a client mount-state fix), STOP and escalate (root §6.5) — this would change the mount contract and needs sign-off.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Restore from Source restores content">
      <steps>
        <step>Open a transient/uploaded doc and edit it.</step>
        <step>Invoke Restore from Source.</step>
        <step>Verify content is restored without blanking or a re-upload prompt.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Restore from Source restores content in place.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Build/test Spaarke.Compose.Components</tool>
